rement\" names the subject action.\n- \"habeas-refactor task\" covers using `habeas-refactor`.\n- \"agreed with the user\" covers the agreement condition.\n- \"committed before its text changes\" covers the ordering.\n\nThe assertion fails if the skill drops any of these, so it enforces the obligation. The check is a text-presence check on static skill content. That is the only observable behavior the requirement governs, and no other input classes or failure cases are named. I found no behavioral gap.",
